<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claudius Gothicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">214–270</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Claudius II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> Gothicus, or Claudius II, was Roman emperor from 268 to 270, one of the soldier emperors of the third-century crisis. Soon after his accession he defeated an Alemannic army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-garda">Lake Garda</a>, and around 269 he won a great victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nis">Naissus</a>, which earned him his surname. He died of plague at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirmium">Sirmium</a> in 270, and the family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine the Great</a> later claimed descent from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/claudius-gothicus.jpg" alt="Claudius Gothicus" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Museum of Fine Arts, Boston · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ClaudiusGothicusSC265569.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
